Dear Mr Moss,

The contractor, Pale Finch Decorating, has now sent his written quotation for the entrance door at 14 Lantern Mews. It is the same quotation we sent you earlier (ref NBL-017-Q1), valid until 28 February 2025.

- Work covered: preparation, sanding, spot filling and repainting of the flat-side face and visible top edge.
- Price: £186.00, including materials and labour.
- Not covered: adjustment of the door, frame or hinges, hardware work, investigation of why the door catches, or any fire-door inspection or fire-safety opinion.

He also confirms that his visit was visual only. It did not include measuring or adjusting the door, or checking its fire performance. So the cause of the catching is still unknown, and painting alone may not cure it. The building file lists the flat entrance doors as fire-resisting, and building management has asked that no drilling or alterations are arranged without checking with them first.

He has not yet told us whether the visit carries a charge. We have asked and will tell you if it does. No cost was approved before the visit, so payment for it will be your decision.

Our separate approval request still stands, with these options: (A) painting only at £186.00; (B) a further inspection of the closing, clearances and hinges, and of the fire-resisting status, by a door specialist, with a price sent to you first; or (C) both in sequence. Please tell us which you would like. Nothing will be booked until you do.

Kind regards,
Northbridge Lettings
